        "id": 1132414
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-13T21:15:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could also do __attribute__((unused)). Linux #defines that as __maybe_unused, which is a good name for it, and that really helps in maintaining highly-configurable codebases.\n\nYou also can get around this by moving it to a header; no modern compilers complain about static inline functions in headers that are unused.\n\nSide note: maybe this *does* belong in a common place (e.g., header), since cortex-m0/task.c seems to have reimplemented the same stuff.",
      "parentUuid": "b14534fd_43a7a0b6",
